Hi everyone, I have some of the design review notes in my handover that might help unblock a few of you:

@eng-54 (METRICORE-104): For EWMA, alpha = 2 / (span + 1). span=3 gives alpha = 0.5, so ewma([0, 8, 8], 3) == [0.0, 4.0, 6.0]; span=1 gives alpha = 1.

@eng-41 (METRICORE-111): For histogram_quantile, if the rank falls into the overflow bucket, return the last finite bound (bounds[-1]). Never return infinity: histogram_quantile(0.99, [100, 250, 500], [50, 30, 10, 10]) == 500.0.

@eng-38, I don't have notes for iqr_outliers, but hopefully these help the others!
